  "routeAdjustment": "Use the proved original meromorphic order map directly. Native cyclic valuation rings and the existing unit/uniformizer factorization give positive integer normalization. Native meromorphic boundedness and Mobius order invariance prove the required dictionary properties. No Puiseux expansion, elliptic torsion, supplied dictionary structure or numerical genus assumption is needed for this prerequisite. The next coordinate consumer connects the literal original j to its analytic value before attempting the finite-place geometry.",
